# neutron-icons-font
#
# Touches: fonts/Makefile.in, fonts/neutron-icons.sfd (new). BINARY, not in this diff: fonts/neutron-icons.ttf -- copy
# fonts2/font/neutron-icons.ttf (sha256 e9b2ca43cb59f39340e31ae32a663daafc5778555a7dc06532f665832e232575) next to the
# .sfd; the build uses the committed .ttf when FONTFORGE is empty (it is in the wine-tkg build), like marlett/tahoma.
# Pairs with the CLI change cli-icon-font.diff (Replacements "Segoe MDL2 Assets" -> "Neutron Icons"; "Segoe Fluent Icons"
# deliberately NOT mapped: no lab app asks it for these glyphs, and Chromium/Qt pick their own drawing when it is absent).
#
# WHAT HAPPENED (lab, 11-05, Topaz Photo 1.7.1): its minimize/maximize/close buttons showed wrong symbols.
# MECHANISM: Topaz's caption buttons are QML text in "Segoe MDL2 Assets" (U+E921 minimize, U+E922 maximize, U+E923 restore,
# U+E8BB close; U+E73E check mark elsewhere) -- read from the compiled QML in Topaz Photo.exe. Wine has no such font, so
# DirectWrite font fallback picked whatever host font has glyphs at those private-use code points (in the lab a Nerd Font).
# FIX: "Neutron Icons", a font of our own with ONLY those 5 glyphs, drawn by fonts2/font/mkfont.py (params-measured.json) from geometric
# primitives (bars, square rings, a mitred polyline); no outline, hint or table from any other font. Installed with Wine's
# fonts (#pragma makedep install -> share/wine/fonts), registered by `neutron prefix provision`/`fonts repair`
# (register_prefix_fonts), reached through HKCU\Software\Wine\Fonts\Replacements, which dwrite and GDI apply only while
# the real font is absent. License LGPL-2.1-or-later, as Wine's own fonts. Microsoft's font is not shipped or copied.
# WINDOWS (v0.2, the Windows test machine 11-06, probe mdl2metrics): Segoe MDL2 Assets em 2048, ascent 2048, descent 0, advance 2048.
# Caption glyphs on a 10x10 grid of the em (unit 204.8): minimize = full-width bar y 1024..1229; maximize = ring of
# the em, stroke 205; restore = front ring 0..1638 (inner 205..1434) + back ring 410..2048 (inner 614..1843), only its
# uncovered part; close = X across the em, perpendicular stroke 205 (edges meet the sides 145 from the corners).
# CheckMark = centre line (256,1024)-(768,512)-(1792,1536) on a 16-unit grid, stroke 128, butt ends, mitred join.
# Only these sizes/positions come from Windows (font/params-measured.json); mkfont.py draws every outline itself (the X
# is now one 12-point union outline computed from the stroke, like Windows' glyph). Output coordinates = Windows'.
# NOT COVERED: any other MDL2 code point and all of Segoe Fluent Icons (fall back as before); QWindowsIconEngine theme icons (qwindows.dll), Qt's
# Windows 11 style (Fluent Icons), Chromium fluent scrollbars -- no app in the lab was seen drawing those.
#
# LAB EVIDENCE v0.2 (11.10-183f, desk l, Topaz prefixes from PgV-tz1 provisioned with smallgaps' CLI, 168 dpi):
#   mapping present 2/2; captures vs Windows' measured outlines rendered at the same em (fonts2/scripts/strokes.py,
#   coverage centroids): normal 2/2 (tzI1-a, tzI2-c) minimize bar centre 0.463 em (Windows 0.456), close bars at 0.329/
#   0.693 em (0.308/0.695); maximized 2/2 (tzI1-b, tzI2-b) restore strokes 0.094/0.754/0.945 (0.049/0.746/0.954) and
#   0.064/0.251/0.910 (0.049/0.249/0.953) -- within ~1 px at a 25-28 px em (desk shot = 1.75 output resampled to 2).
#   All strokes equal (bar 2.48, ring 2.46, X 2.55 px; Windows: one stroke for all); shots/icons-vs-windows.png.
#   v0.1 lab evidence (smallgaps, 183g): mapped right glyphs 2/2 + restore 2/2; unmapped wrong glyphs 2/2.
#   Check mark (E73E) not seen in Topaz before sign-in.
# Kill switch: remove the Replacements value (or `fonts check` shows icon-font "warn" until repaired).
--- a/fonts/Makefile.in
+++ b/fonts/Makefile.in
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 	marlett.sfd \
 	ms_sans_serif.sfd \
 	msyh.sfd \
+	neutron-icons.sfd \
 	small_fonts.sfd \
 	small_fonts_jp.sfd \
 	symbol.sfd \
--- a/fonts/neutron-icons.sfd
+++ b/fonts/neutron-icons.sfd
@@ -0,0 +1,215 @@
